Architecture plan for Issue #232: Link the footer logo to https://ideavibes.ai/

Scope and module structure
- Shared footer partial:
  - `rust-backend/templates/partials/footer.html` owns the footer logo, tagline, and newsletter form.
  - Issue #232 should update only the footer logo anchor `href` from the local blog root (`/`) to the external Ideavibes homepage (`https://ideavibes.ai/`).
- Header partial:
  - `rust-backend/templates/partials/header.html` owns the top navigation logo.
  - It is intentionally out of scope; the header logo should continue linking to the blog home page unless the issue explicitly says otherwise.
- Layout/rendering:
  - `rust-backend/templates/layout.html` includes the footer partial on every public/admin page, so changing the partial applies globally without touching Rust context structs or shared types.
- Tests/build:
  - Existing HTML rendering tests live under `rust-backend/src/html/mod.rs`.
  - If there is an assertion expecting the footer logo link to be `/`, update it to expect `https://ideavibes.ai/`.
  - Validate with the plain Rust backend build/test path (`cargo build --manifest-path rust-backend/Cargo.toml` or `npm run backend:test`). No Tailwind rebuild is needed because the change is an href only.

Dependencies between issues
- This batch contains only Issue #232.
- It builds on prior logo sizing work but does not depend on additional CSS, database, storage, auth, or routing changes.
- The footer-only change is independent of post rendering, Markdown rendering, and attribution-card layout.

Key design decisions
- Product brand remains Ideavibes as stated by the issue and existing templates.
- Use a normal absolute URL with trailing slash: `https://ideavibes.ai/`.
- Keep the hosted logo image `src`, `alt`, dimensions, and display classes unchanged.
- Avoid adding `target="_blank"` unless explicitly requested; the issue only asks to link to the URL.
